      "question": {
        ":question/id": "3ca6bef9-97a0-5f2c-9c76-b5e54d50b32e",
        ":question/problem": "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $X$ into the matrix $W$, where\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,W=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 9\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that the $2$nd and the $1$st rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $3$rd row. \n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $3$rd row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+4\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =W.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+4{R}_{2}.\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "fcda73cf-e00c-5aa7-ae46-c033681d0fca",
