      "question": {
        ":question/id": "ed847934-cdb4-5163-a810-fe58052a6d71",
        ":question/problem": "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $E$ into the matrix $F$, where\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,F=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that the $2$nd row is the same in both matrices. The only rows that have changed are the $3$rd row and the $1$st row.   \n\nBy considering the given row operations that change both the $3$rd and the $1$st row, we notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 7\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}\u2194{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =F.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}\u2194{R}_{1}.\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
